e  trying to  trying to detect rare variants  okay thank you  um next why are chimeric fragments  problematic for data analysis  yeah um so  a chimeric bright i guess the there's  the data quality issues that i discussed  um during the talk um but in really  simple terms what uh aligning chimeras  um during during analysis uh actually is  a lot slower just because of how it has  to find i guess the position to find the  alignments so minimizing the the amount  of chimeras ultimately means that you  can process data faster  great thank you  um next question  can you generate less than six kb  libraries for long red sequencing with  this kit  um  it was not developed to do that um and  we haven't uh we haven't done any  testing on uh those uh at those sorts of  lengths um like i mentioned before this  was this is really just uh developed for  um use on illumina short read platform  all right  um next question  do you have  automation script or method already  developed for your library prep if so  for which liquid handler  yeah great question um uh unfortunately  we don't have anything specific uh right  now and uh we haven't worked on any  specific platform uh as of right now um  we do have some uh i guess some  relationships or some of our commercial  relationships that are uh we're starting  to work through stuff like that and i  think just um just to make the the point  i suppose  uh we're always happy to work with  um you or work with a customer on  facilitating that sort of um  developing those sorts of scripts  um  also just as a note any  if you already have  scripts or if there's already scripts  for whatever platform you're looking for  that that work with other  um similar types of library prep kits um  then those are generally good places to  start um  uh yeah i think that's the answer there  all right  um well thank you zane for your time  today and your important research  we would also like to thank lab roots  and our sponsor watchmaker genomics for  un